          "summary": "The administration’s 278,000 figure appears to combine its claim of more than 250,000 potential noncitizens in four states with 28,000 more in 23 cooperating states. The central dispute is not whether noncitizens may ever appear on rolls, but whether the matching process reliably establishes citizenship and registration status.",
